window.__F=window.__F||{};window.__F["acc-32.html"]="<div class=\"ac-info\"><p class=\"ac-i-main\">تشخيص عقل باب الراكب PDM: يشبه عقل السائق DDM: المرآة والشبابيك والأقفال.</p><p class=\"ac-i-tip\"><b>متى تستعمله:</b> اتبع الفحص المسبق Pre-Diagnostic ثم خطوات كل كود.</p><div class=\"ac-chips\"><span class=\"en-chip\">B = كهرباء الجسم: 40</span><span class=\"en-chip\">U = اتصال الشبكة: 4</span></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong>كيف تقرأ كود العطل</strong><small>الرقم بعد الشرطة يدل على نوع العطل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-legend\"><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-11</b><span>قصر على الأرضي</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-12</b><span>قصر على البطارية</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-13</b><span>دائرة مفتوحة</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-15</b><span>قصر على البطارية أو دائرة مفتوحة</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-16</b><span>الفولتية أقل من الحد</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-17</b><span>الفولتية أعلى من الحد</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-2A</b><span>مفتاح عالق Stuck</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-84 / 85</b><span>الإشارة أقل / أعلى من المدى</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-92</b><span>أداء ضعيف أو تشغيل غير صحيح</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-00</b><span>عطل عام أو بدون نوع محدد</span></div></div><p class=\"bcm-note\">الحرف الأول: B = كهرباء الجسم · C = الهيكل والحساسات · P = نقل الحركة · U = اتصال الشبكة. نفّذ دائماً الفحص المسبق Pre-Diagnostic قبل خطوات أي كود.</p></div></details></div><input type=\"search\" class=\"ec-search acc-q\" placeholder=\"ابحث: كود العطل أو كلمة من الوصف\" aria-label=\"بحث\"><p class=\"bcm-note acc-cnt\">44 كود عطل. اضغط على الكود لترى شرحه.</p><div class=\"acc-list\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b173d-11 mirror signal lamp control - circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B173D-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">MIRROR SIGNAL LAMP CONTROL - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">On-demand.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module senses a short to ground on the Mirror Turn Signal Driver circuit for more than two seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Turn Signal Lamp in the Mirror is inoperative.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>OUTSIDE REAR VIEW MIRROR FAULTY WIRING</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE FAULTY WIRING</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, record and erase the DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the passenger side turn signal on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the park lamps on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the rear defogger on, if equipped with heated mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Press and release the Mirror Select switch to select the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Operate the Mirror Adjust switch in all directions several times while monitoring the scan tool for DTCs in the PDM.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           After adjusting the mirror in one direction wait at least two seconds before adjusting the mirror in the opposite direction, as this will allow time for an active fault to set if present.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, read the DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (P502) PASSENGER MIRROR TURN SIGNAL DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Door Module C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (P502) Passenger Mirror Turn Signal Driver circuit at the Passenger Door Module C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (P502) Passenger Mirror Turn Signal Driver circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P502) Passenger Mirror Turn Signal Driver circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK (P502) PASSENGER MIRROR TURN SIGNAL DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO ANOTHER CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (P502) Passenger Mirror Turn Signal Driver circuit and all other circuits at the Passenger Door Module C2 connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (P502) Passenger Mirror Turn Signal Driver circuit and any other circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P502) Passenger Mirror Turn Signal Driver circuit for a short to the other circuit. If no problems are found, replace the Outside Rearview Mirror Assembly in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MIRROR, OUTSIDE REARVIEW, GLASS, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>MIRROR OR MODULE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, record and erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the passengers side turn signal on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Operate the Fold and Unfold switch several time, if equipped with folding mirrors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the rear defogger on, if equipped with heated mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the park lamps on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Press and release the Mirror Select switch to select the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Operate the Mirror Adjust switch in all directions several times while monitoring the scan tool for DTCs in the PDM.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           After adjusting the mirror in one direction wait at least two seconds before adjusting the mirror in the opposite direction, as this will allow time for an active fault to set if present.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check for a change in DTCs.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Outside Rearview Mirror Assembly in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to MIRROR, OUTSIDE REARVIEW, GLASS, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b173d-12 mirror signal lamp control - circuit short to battery\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B173D-12</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">MIRROR SIGNAL LAMP CONTROL - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Continuous.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module senses a short to battery on the Mirror Turn Signal Driver circuit for more than two seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Turn Signal Lamp in the Mirror is inoperative.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>MIRROR TURN SIGNAL DRIVER CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>OUTSIDE REAR VIEW MIRROR</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the turn signals to be sure they are flashing properly before proceeding.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, record and erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the passenger side turn signal on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the park lamps on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the rear defogger on, if equipped with heated mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Press and release the Mirror Select switch to select the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Operate the Mirror Adjust switch in all directions several times while monitoring the scan tool for DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           After adjusting the mirror in one direction wait at least two seconds before adjusting the mirror in the opposite direction, as this will allow time for an active fault to set if present.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (P502) PASSENGER MIRROR TURN SIGNAL DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO ANY SIGNAL OR DRIVER CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn all accessories off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror C1 (Component Side) and C2 (Component Side) harness connectors from the Door Module.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for continuity between the (P502) Passenger Mirror Turn Signal Driver circuit and any Signal or Driver circuit at the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror C1 and C2 (Component Side) harness connectors.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (P502) Passenger Mirror Turn Signal Driver circuit and any Signal or Driver circuit(s)?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P502) Passenger Mirror Turn Signal Driver circuit for a short to any Signal or Driver circuit(s).</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>MIRROR OR MODULE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Replace the Outside Rearview Mirror Assembly in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MIRROR, OUTSIDE REARVIEW, GLASS, REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, record and erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the passenger side turn signal on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the park lamps on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the rear defogger on, if equipped with heated mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Press and release the Mirror Select switch to select the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Operate the Mirror Adjust switch in all directions several times while monitoring the scan tool for DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           After adjusting the mirror in one direction wait at least two seconds before adjusting the mirror in the opposite direction, as this will allow time for an active fault to set if present.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b173d-13 mirror signal lamp control - circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B173D-13</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">MIRROR SIGNAL LAMP CONTROL - CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Continuous.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module senses an open between the Mirror Turn Signal Driver circuit and the Mirror Turn Signal Return circuit for more than two seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Turn Signal Lamp in the Mirror is inoperative.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>MIRROR TURN SIGNAL DRIVER CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>OUTSIDE REAR VIEW MIRROR</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, record and erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the passenger side turn signal on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Press and release the Mirror Select switch to select the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (P502) PASSENGER MIRROR TURN SIGNAL DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN TO THE (P595) PASSENGER MIRROR TURN SIGNAL RETURN CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn all accessories off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror C1 (Component Side) and C2 (Component Side) harness connectors from the Door Module.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for continuity between the (P502) Passenger Mirror Turn Signal Driver circuit and the (P595) Passenger Mirror Turn Signal Return circuit at the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror C2 (Component Side) harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (P502) Passenger Mirror Turn Signal Driver circuit and the (P595) Passenger Mirror Turn Signal Return circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P502) Passenger Mirror Turn Signal Driver circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>MIRROR OR MODULE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Replace the Outside Rearview Mirror Assembly in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MIRROR, OUTSIDE REARVIEW, GLASS, REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, record and erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the passenger side turn signal on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Press and release the Mirror Select switch to select the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1751-11 courtesy lamp control - circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1751-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">COURTESY LAMP CONTROL - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The courtesy lamp is a LED with a built in circuit board. The BCM controls the operation and sends a bus message to the Door Module to turn the lamp on or off.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The Courtesy (door trim) lamp is on.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The configured Courtesy (door trim) lamp is true.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module detects a short to ground on the Courtesy Lamp Driver circuit.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Courtesy Lamp is inoperative.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>DOOR COURTESY LAMP DRIVER CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>DOOR COURTESY LAMP DRIVER CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE DOOR LIGHTING RETURN</li><li>CIRCUIT</li><li>DOOR LAMP (TRIM/PUDDLE)</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Lower the Passenger window.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on to off three times.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Close the doors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Open the Passenger door.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Turn the ignition on and wait one minute.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE PASSENGER DOOR (TRIM/PUDDLE) LAMP FOR A SHORT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, erase the DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Remove the inner door panel trim in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Door Courtesy (trim/puddle) Lamp connector if it is not already disconnected.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Close then open the Passenger door.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Wait one minute.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Courtesy (trim/puddle) Lamp Assembly.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (M44) PASSENGER DOOR COURTESY LAMP DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Door Module C5 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (M44) Passenger Door Courtesy Lamp Driver circuit at the Passenger Door Module C5 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (M44) Passenger Door Courtesy Lamp Driver circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (M44) Passenger Door Courtesy Lamp Driver circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (M44) PASSENGER DOOR COURTESY LAMP DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO THE (M36) PASSENGER DOOR LIGHTING RETURN CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (M44) Passenger Door Courtesy Lamp Driver circuit and the (M36) Passenger Door Lighting Return circuit at the Passenger Door Module C5 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (M44) Passenger Door Courtesy Lamp Driver circuit and the (M36) Passenger Door Lighting Return circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (M44) Passenger Door Courtesy Lamp Driver circuit for a short to the (M36) Passenger Door Lighting Return circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1751-15 courtesy lamp control - circuit short to battery or open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1751-15</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">COURTESY LAMP CONTROL - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY OR OPEN</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية أو دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The courtesy lamp is a LED with a built in circuit board. The BCM controls the operation and sends a bus message to the Door Module to turn the lamp on or off.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The Courtesy (door trim) lamp is on.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The configured Courtesy (door trim) lamp is true.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Courtesy Lamp Driver circuit is on when it should be off or off when it should be on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Incorrect Courtesy Lamp operation.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>DOOR COURTESY LAMP DRIVER CIRCUIT SHORTED TO BATTERY</li><li>DOOR COURTESY LAMP CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>DOOR LAMP</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Lower the passenger door window.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on to off three times.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Close then open the passenger door.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Wait one minute.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (M44) PASSENGER DOOR COURTESY LAMP DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Remove the inner door panel trim in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Door Module C5 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (M44) Passenger Door Ambient Lamp Driver circuit at the Passenger Door Module C5 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (M44) Passenger Door Courtesy Lamp Driver circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (M44) PASSENGER DOOR COURTESY LAMP DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Make sure the Passenger Door Courtesy (puddle/trim) Lamp connector is still connected.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect a fused jumper wire between B(+), to the (M44) Passenger Door Courtesy Lamp Driver circuit at the Passenger Door Module C5 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Connect a jumper wire between ground and the (M36) Passenger Door Lighting Return circuit at the Passenger Door Module C5 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the Passenger Door Courtesy (puddle/trim) Lamp illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (M44) PASSENGER DOOR COURTESY LAMP DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Door Puddle Lamp harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (M44) Passenger Door Courtesy Lamp Driver circuit between the PDM C5 harness connector and the Passenger Door Courtesy (puddle/trim) Lamp harness connector at the Passenger Door Module C5 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 2.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (M44) Passenger Door Courtesy Lamp Driver circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (M36) PASSENGER DOOR LIGHTING RETURN CIRCUIT FOR A OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (M36) Passenger Door Lighting Return circuit between the Passenger Door Module C5 harness connector and the Passenger Door Courtesy (puddle/trim) Lamp harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 2.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Courtesy (puddle/trim) Lamp.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (M36) Passenger Door Lighting Return circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b18ba-11 window control - circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B18BA-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">WINDOW CONTROL - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If both of the Window Driver circuits (Up and Down) are grounded during a window movement command, the motor will be totally inoperative. To lower the window, voltage is applied to the Window Driver (Down) circuit and the Window Driver (UP) circuit remains grounded in the module. To drive the window up, the circuits are reversed.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Continuous.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module detects the Window Driver circuit(s) Up/Down is grounded.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The window will move only in one direction.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>WINDOW DRIVER DOWN CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>WINDOW DRIVER UP CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>DRIVER WINDOW MOTOR</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Try to operate the Passenger Window up and down several times.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Wait 30 seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE WINDOW MOTOR FOR A SHORT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, erase the DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Window Motor connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Operate the passenger window switch up and down several times.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Wait 30 seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Window Motor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MOTOR, WINDOW REGULATOR, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (Q22) PASSENGER WINDOW DRIVER DOWN CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Door Module C4 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (Q22) Passenger Window Driver Down circuit at the Passenger Door Module C4 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (Q22) Passenger Window Driver Down circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Q22) Passenger Window Driver Down circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (Q12) PASSENGER WINDOW DRIVER UP CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (Q12) Passenger Window Driver Up circuit at the Passenger Door Module C4 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (Q12) Passenger Window Driver Up circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Q12) Passenger Window Driver Up circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (Q22) PASSENGER WINDOW DRIVER DOWN CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO (Q12) PASSENGER WINDOW DRIVER UP CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (Q22) Passenger Window Driver Down circuit and the (Q12) Passenger Window Driver Up circuit at the Passenger Door Module C4 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (Q22) Passenger Window Driver Down circuit and the (Q12) Passenger Window Driver Up circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Q22) Passenger Window Driver Down circuit for a short to the (Q12) Passenger Window Driver Up circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b18ba-12 window control - circuit short to battery\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B18BA-12</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">WINDOW CONTROL - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If either one of the Window Driver circuits are shorted to battery, the motor will operative in one direction only. If the current remains on when the window is in its full travel, the circuit breaker will open. To lower the window, voltage is applied to the Window Driver (Down) circuit and the Window Driver (UP) circuit remains grounded in the module. To drive the window up, the circuits are reversed.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Continuous.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module detects the Window Driver circuit(s) Up/Down are supplied with voltage.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Incorrect window operation.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Possible battery draw by the Door Module not going into sleep mode.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>WINDOW DRIVER DOWN CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>WINDOW DRIVER UP CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>DRIVER WINDOW MOTOR</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Try to operate the Passenger Window up and down several times.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Wait 30 seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE WINDOW MOTOR FOR A SHORT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, erase the DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Window Motor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Operate the Passenger window switch up and down several times.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Wait 30 seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Window Motor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MOTOR, WINDOW REGULATOR, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (Q22) PASSENGER WINDOW DRIVER DOWN CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Door Module C4 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (Q22) Passenger Window Driver Down circuit at the Passenger Door Module C4 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Q22) Passenger Window Driver Down circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (Q12) PASSENGER WINDOW DRIVER UP CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage between the (Q12) Passenger Window Driver Up circuit and ground at the Passenger Door Module C4 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Q12) Passenger Window Driver Up circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b18ba-13 window control - circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B18BA-13</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">WINDOW CONTROL - CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The microprocessor-based electronic Passenger Door Module (PDM) contains logic circuits that monitor various hard wired low current, multiplexed inputs from the power window, power lock, power mirror and memory switches. The program logic within the PDM allows the microprocessor to prioritize all inputs and then determine the tasks it needs to perform. These tasks are then completed either by controlling hard wired outputs to the various motors, actuators or lamps on its own or by sending electronic message requests over the CAN- IHS Bus to the appropriate electronic module in the vehicle.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The Bus is awake.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The window motor is continuously requested to move repeatedly without a sufficient cooling time (1-2 seconds).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module logic has determined the temperature of the window motor has exceeded 80°C (176°F).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Window is inoperative.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>HIGH TEMPERATURE FAILURE</li><li>PASSENGER DOOR WINDOW MOTOR</li><li>PASSENGER DOOR MODULE (PDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CONFIRM WINDOW OPERATION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Run the window to the full up position and continue to hold the switch for an additional two seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Run the window to the full down position and continue to hold the switch for an additional two seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Repeat the above procedures again.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the window move to the full up position?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE WINDOW MOTOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Window Motor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect a 12 volt test light between the (Q12) Passenger Window Passenger Up circuit and the (Q22) Passenger Window Passenger Down circuit at the Passenger Window Motor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Trip the Passenger door latch to the closed position.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Operate the Passenger window switch up and down several times while observing the test light.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly when the switch is pressed in both directions?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test Complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Window Motor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MOTOR, WINDOW REGULATOR, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b18e6-2a window switch - stuck\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B18E6-2A</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">WINDOW SWITCH - STUCK</small><small>العطل: عالق (Stuck)</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The microprocessor-based electronic Passenger Door Module (PDM) contains logic circuits that monitor various hard wired low current, multiplexed inputs from the power window, power lock, power mirror and memory switches. The program logic within the PDM allows the microprocessor to prioritize all inputs and then determine the tasks it needs to perform. These tasks are then completed either by controlling hard wired outputs to the various motors, actuators or lamps on its own or by sending electronic message requests over the CAN- IHS Bus to the appropriate electronic module in the vehicle.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The Bus is awake.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The Door Module is configured as the Passenger side.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module detects a Front Right Window signal from the Passenger Window Switch for more than 30 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Incorrect window operation. All other switches operate normally.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>PASSENGER WINDOW SWITCH MUX CIRCUIT PARTIAL SHORT TO GROUND</li><li>PASSENGER WINDOW SWITCH MUX CIRCUIT SHORT TO THE PASSENGER WINDOW</li><li>SWITCH RETURN CIRCUIT</li><li>WINDOW/DOOR LOCK SWITCH SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>PASSENGER DOOR MODULE (PDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Operate the Passenger Window Switch in all positions several times.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Wait 30 seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE PASSENGER WINDOW SWITCH FOR A SHORT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, erase the DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Window/Door Lock Switch harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Window/Door Lock Switch in accordance with Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to SWITCH, POWER WINDOW, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (Q336) PASSENGER WINDOW SWITCH MUX CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Door Module C5 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (Q336) Passenger Window Switch Mux circuit at the Passenger Door Module C5 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (Q336) Passenger Window Switch Mux circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Q336) Passenger Window Switch Mux circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (Q336) PASSENGER WINDOW SWITCH MUX CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO THE (Q936) PASSENGER WINDOW SWITCH RETURN CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (Q336) Passenger Window Switch Mux circuit and the (Q936) Passenger Window Switch Return circuit at the Passenger Door Module C5 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (Q336) Passenger Window Switch Mux circuit and the (Q936) Passenger Window Switch Return circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Q336) Passenger Switch Mux circuit for a short to the (Q936) Passenger Window Switch Return circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1dd0-11 mirror heater control - circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1DD0-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">MIRROR HEATER CONTROL - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When the Door Module receives a CAN bus message from the HVAC Module, the Door Module will activate or deactivate the Heated Mirror Feed Driver circuit.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Continuous.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module detects a short to ground on the Mirror Heater Driver circuit.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Heated Mirror is inoperative.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>MIRROR HEATER DRIVER CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>DRIVER OUTSIDE REARVIEW MIRROR</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the hazard lamps on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the heated mirrors on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the park lamps on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Press and release the Mirror Select switch to select the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Operate the Mirror Adjust switch in all directions several times while monitoring the scan tool for DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           After adjusting the mirror in one direction wait at least two seconds before adjusting the mirror in the opposite direction, as this will allow time for an active fault to set if present.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The conditions that caused this code to set are not present at this time. For vehicle&#x27;s equipped with folding outside rearview mirrors, repeat test with mirror folded. If no trouble found, use the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide and inspect the wiring and connectors.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE MIRROR CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror C3 and C4 connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Door Module C2 connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect the wiring harness, connectors and the Passenger Door Module.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Check for cracks in the mirror glass.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK (C17) PASSENGER MIRROR HEATER DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO ANOTHER CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (C17) Passenger Mirror Heater Driver circuit and all other circuits at the Passenger Door Module C2 connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (C17) Passenger Mirror Heater Driver circuit and any other circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (C17) Passenger Mirror Heater Driver circuit for a short any other circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE MIRROR OR MODULE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, record and erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the drivers side turn signal on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Fold and unfold the mirrors several time, if equipped with folding mirrors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the rear defogger on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the park lamps on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Press and release the Mirror Select switch to select the Driver Outside Rearview Mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Operate the Mirror Adjust switch in all directions several times while monitoring the scan tool for DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           After adjusting the mirror in one direction wait at least two seconds before adjusting the mirror in the opposite direction, as this will allow time for an active fault to set if present.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check for a change in status to this DTC as.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Outside Rearview Mirror Assembly in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to MIRROR, OUTSIDE REARVIEW, GLASS, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1dd0-15 mirror heater control - circuit short to battery or open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1DD0-15</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">MIRROR HEATER CONTROL - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY OR OPEN</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية أو دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When the Door Module receives a CAN bus message from the HVAC Module, the Door Module will activate or deactivate the Heated Mirror Feed Driver circuit.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">On-demand.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module detects an open or a short to battery on the Mirror Heater Driver circuit.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Heated Mirror is inoperative or will not turn off.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>MIRROR HEATER DRIVER CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>DRIVER OUTSIDE REAR VIEW MIRROR</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, record and erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the turn signal on, if equipped with turn signal mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the approach lamps on, if equipped.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the rear defogger on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Press and release the Mirror Select switch to select the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Operate the Mirror Adjust switch in all directions several times while monitoring the scan tool for DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           After adjusting the mirror in one direction wait at least two seconds before adjusting the mirror in the opposite direction, as this will allow time for an active fault to set if present.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, read the DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (C17) PASSENGER MIRROR HEATER DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror C2 (Component Side) connector from the Door Module C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (C17) Passenger Mirror Heater Driver circuit in the</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Driver Outside Rearview Mirror C2 (Component Side) connector.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (C17) Passenger Mirror Heater Driver circuit for a short to voltage. If the wiring harness and connector are okay, replace the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MIRROR, OUTSIDE REARVIEW, GLASS, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (C17) PASSENGER MIRROR HEATER DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO ANOTHER MIRROR DRIVER CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (C17) Passenger Mirror Heater Driver circuit and all of the Mirror Driver circuits in the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror C2 (Component Side) connectors.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (C17) Passenger Mirror Heater Driver circuit and all of the Mirror Driver circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair all circuits with continuity for a short to the (C17) Passenger Mirror Heater Driver circuit. If the wiring harness and connector are okay, replace the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MIRROR, OUTSIDE REARVIEW, GLASS, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all PDM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw).</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity. Check for spread terminals and verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect all PDM harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the when monitored and set conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Inspect the wiring and connectors for damage and repair as necessary. If the wiring and connectors are okay, replace the Door Module in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL . Test complete. Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Test complete. Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1f02-11 mirror vertical motor control - circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1F02-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">MIRROR VERTICAL MOTOR CONTROL - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Mirror Vertical Driver circuit supplies battery voltage for the mirror up position and ground for the mirror down position. The Mirror Common Driver supplies battery voltage for the mirror Down position and ground for the mirror up position.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">On-demand.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module detects a short to ground on the Mirror Vertical Driver circuit.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Mirror is inoperative.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>MIRROR VERTICAL DRIVER CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>DRIVER OUTSIDE REARVIEW MIRROR</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Press and release the Mirror Select switch to select the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the hazard lamps on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn on the park lamps (if equipped with auto dimming mirrors).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the rear defogger on, if equipped with heated mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Operate the Mirror Adjust switch in all directions several times while monitoring the scan tool for DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           After adjusting the mirror in one direction wait at least two seconds before adjusting the mirror in the opposite direction, as this will allow time for an active fault to set if present.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The conditions that caused this code to set are not present at this time. For vehicle&#x27;s equipped with folding outside rearview mirrors, repeat test with mirror folded. If no problems are found, use the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide and inspect the wiring and connectors.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (P72) PASSENGER MIRROR VERTICAL DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Door Module C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (P72) Passenger Mirror Vertical Driver circuit at the Passenger Door Module C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (P72) Passenger Mirror Vertical Driver circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P72) Passenger Mirror Vertical Driver circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK (P72) PASSENGER MIRROR VERTICAL DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO ANOTHER CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (P72) Passenger Mirror Vertical Driver circuit and all other circuits at the Passenger Door Module C2 connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (P72) Passenger Mirror Vertical Driver circuit and any other circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P72) Passenger Mirror Vertical Driver circuit for a short. If no problems are found, replace the Outside Rearview Mirror Assembly in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MIRROR, OUTSIDE REARVIEW, GLASS, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all PDM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity. Check for spread terminals and verify proper terminal tension.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect all PDM harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the when monitored and set conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Outside Rearview Mirror Assembly in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Refer to MIRROR, OUTSIDE REARVIEW, GLASS, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1f02-12 mirror vertical motor control - circuit short to battery\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1F02-12</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">MIRROR VERTICAL MOTOR CONTROL - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Mirror Vertical Driver circuit supplies battery voltage for the mirror up position and ground for the mirror down position. The Mirror Common Driver supplies battery voltage for the mirror Down position and ground for the mirror up position.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">On-demand.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module detects a short to battery on the Mirror Vertical Driver circuit.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Mirror is inoperative.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>DRIVER OUTSIDE REARVIEW MIRROR</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM) WIRING</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Press and release the Mirror Select switch to select the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Operate the Mirror Adjust switch in all directions several times.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the ignition from on to off three times.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">The conditions that caused this code to set are not present at this time. For vehicles equipped with folding outside rearview mirrors, repeat test with mirror folded. If no problems are found, use the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide and inspect the wiring and connectors.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (P72) PASSENGER MIRROR VERTICAL DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the harness connector at the component of the circuit being tested. Note: Use the wiring diagram as a guide to follow the path of the circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using a DVOM, measure the voltage of the circuit being tested at the component harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (P72) PASSENGER MIRROR VERTICAL DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO ANOTHER CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Door Module C2 connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between the (P72) Passenger Mirror Vertical Driver circuit and all other circuits at the Passenger Door Module C2 connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (P72) Passenger Mirror Vertical Driver circuit and any other circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all PDM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity. Check for spread terminals and verify proper terminal tension.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect all PDM harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the when monitored and set conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Outside Rearview Mirror Assembly in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Refer to MIRROR, OUTSIDE REARVIEW, GLASS, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1f02-13 mirror vertical motor control - circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1F02-13</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">MIRROR VERTICAL MOTOR CONTROL - CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Mirror Vertical Driver circuit supplies battery voltage for the mirror up position and ground for the mirror down position. The Mirror Common Driver supplies battery voltage for the mirror Down position and ground for the mirror up position.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">On-demand.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module detects an open on the Mirror Vertical Driver circuit.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Mirror is inoperative.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>MIRROR VERTICAL DRIVER CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>DRIVER OUTSIDE REARVIEW MIRROR</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Press and release the Mirror Select switch to select the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the hazard lamps on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn on the park lamps (if equipped with auto dimming mirrors).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the rear defogger on, if equipped with heated mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Operate the Mirror Adjust switch in all directions several times while monitoring the scan tool for DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           After adjusting the mirror in one direction wait at least two seconds before adjusting the mirror in the opposite direction, as this will allow time for an active fault to set if present.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The conditions that caused this code to set are not present at this time. For vehicle&#x27;s equipped with folding outside rearview mirrors, repeat test with mirror folded. If no problems are found, use the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide and inspect the wiring and connectors.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (P72) PASSENGER MIRROR VERTICAL DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Door Module C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (P72) Passenger Mirror Vertical Driver circuit between the Passenger Door Module C2 connector and the Passenger Mirror harness connector at the Passenger Door Module C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 2.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P72) Passenger Mirror Vertical Driver circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE MIRROR AND HARNESS FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Gain access to the Passenger Door Module but do not disconnect the connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With a 12-volt test light, back probe and connect one lead to the (P72) Passenger Mirror Vertical Driver circuit and the other lead to the (P70) Passenger Mirror Common Driver circuit in the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror (Component Side) connector (PDM C2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>While moving the mirror adjust switch left and right, observe the test light.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly when the switch is moved in either direction?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Outside Rearview Mirror Assembly in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to MIRROR, OUTSIDE REARVIEW, GLASS, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all PDM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity. Check for spread terminals and verify proper terminal tension.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect all PDM harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the when monitored and set conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Test complete. Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1f03-11 mirror horizontal motor control - circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1F03-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">MIRROR HORIZONTAL MOTOR CONTROL - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Mirror Horizontal Driver circuit supplies battery voltage for the mirror left position and ground for the mirror right position. The Mirror Common Driver supplies battery voltage for the mirror right position and ground for the mirror left.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">On-demand.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module detects a short to ground on the Mirror Horizontal Driver circuit.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Mirror is inoperative.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>MIRROR HORIZONTAL DRIVER CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>DRIVER OUTSIDE REARVIEW MIRROR</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Press and release the Mirror Select switch to select the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the hazard lamps on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn on the park lamps (if equipped with auto dimming mirrors).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the rear defogger on, if equipped with heated mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Operate the Mirror Adjust switch in all directions several times while monitoring the scan tool for DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           After adjusting the mirror in one direction wait at least two seconds before adjusting the mirror in the opposite direction, as this will allow time for an active fault to set if present.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The conditions that caused this code to set are not present at this time. For vehicle&#x27;s equipped with folding outside rearview mirrors, repeat test with mirror folded. If no problems are found, use the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide and inspect the wiring and connectors.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (P74) PASSENGER MIRROR HORIZONTAL DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Door Module C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (P74) Passenger Mirror Horizontal Driver circuit at the Passenger Door Module C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (P74) Passenger Mirror Horizontal Driver circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P74) Passenger Mirror Horizontal Driver circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK (P74) PASSENGER MIRROR HORIZONTAL DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO ANOTHER CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (P74) Passenger Mirror Horizontal Driver circuit and all other circuits at the Passenger Door Module C2 connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (P74) Passenger Mirror Horizontal Driver circuit and any other circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P74) Passenger Mirror Horizontal Driver circuit for a short. If no problems are found, replace the Outside Rearview Mirror Assembly in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MIRROR, OUTSIDE REARVIEW, GLASS, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all PDM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity. Check for spread terminals and verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect all PDM harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the when monitored and set conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Outside Rearview Mirror Assembly in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Refer to MIRROR, OUTSIDE REARVIEW, GLASS, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1f03-12 mirror horizontal motor control - circuit short to battery\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1F03-12</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">MIRROR HORIZONTAL MOTOR CONTROL - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Mirror Horizontal Driver circuit supplies battery voltage for the mirror left position and ground for the mirror right position. The Mirror Common Driver supplies battery voltage for the mirror right position and ground for the mirror left.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">On-demand.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module detects a short to battery on the Mirror Horizontal Driver circuit.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Mirror is inoperative.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>MIRROR HORIZONTAL DRIVER CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>DRIVER OUTSIDE REARVIEW MIRROR</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Press and release the Mirror Select switch to select the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the hazard lamps on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn on the park lamps (if equipped with auto dimming mirrors).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the rear defogger on, if equipped with heated mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Operate the Mirror Adjust switch in all directions several times while monitoring the scan tool for DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           After adjusting the mirror in one direction wait at least two seconds before adjusting the mirror in the opposite direction, as this will allow time for an active fault to set if present.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The conditions that caused this code to set are not present at this time. For vehicles equipped with folding outside rearview mirrors, repeat test with mirror folded. If no problems are found, use the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide and inspect the wiring and connectors.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (P74) PASSENGER MIRROR HORIZONTAL DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the harness connector at the component of the circuit being tested. Note: Use the wiring diagram as a guide to follow the path of the circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using a DVOM, measure the voltage of the circuit being tested at the component harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (P74) PASSENGER MIRROR HORIZONTAL DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO ANOTHER CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Door Module C2 connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between the (P74) Passenger Mirror Horizontal Driver circuit and all other circuits at the Passenger Door Module C2 connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (P74) Passenger Mirror Horizontal Driver circuit and any other circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P74) Passenger Mirror Horizontal Driver circuit for a short to another circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all PDM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity. Check for spread terminals and verify proper terminal tension.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect all PDM harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">and the connector locks are fully engaged.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the when monitored and set conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Outside Rearview Mirror Assembly in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Refer to MIRROR, OUTSIDE REARVIEW, GLASS, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1f03-13 mirror horizontal motor control - circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1F03-13</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">MIRROR HORIZONTAL MOTOR CONTROL - CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Mirror Horizontal Driver circuit supplies battery voltage for the mirror left position and ground for the mirror right position. The Mirror Common Driver supplies battery voltage for the mirror right position and ground for the mirror left.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">On-demand.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module detects an open on the Mirror Horizontal Driver circuit.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Mirror is inoperative.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>MIRROR HORIZONTAL DRIVER CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>MIRROR COMMON DRIVER CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>DRIVER OUTSIDE REARVIEW MIRROR</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Press and release the Mirror Select switch to select the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Operate the Mirror Adjust switch in all directions several times.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the ignition from on to off three times.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The conditions that caused this code to set are not present at this time. For vehicle&#x27;s equipped with folding outside rearview mirrors, repeat test with mirror folded. If no problems are found, use the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide and inspect the wiring and connectors.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (P72) PASSENGER MIRROR VERTICAL DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Door Module C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (P72) Passenger Mirror Vertical Driver circuit between the Passenger Door Module C2 connector and the Passenger Mirror harness connector at the Passenger Door Module C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 2.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P72) Passenger Mirror Vertical Driver circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE MIRROR AND HARNESS FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Gain access to the Passenger Door Module but do not disconnect the connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With a 12-volt test light, back probe and connect one lead to the (P74) Passenger Mirror Horizontal Driver circuit and the other lead to the (P70) Passenger Mirror Common Driver circuit in the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror (Component Side) connector (PDM C2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>While moving the mirror adjust switch left and right, observe the test light.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly when the switch is moved in either direction?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Outside Rearview Mirror Assembly in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to MIRROR, OUTSIDE REARVIEW, GLASS, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all PDM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity. Check for spread terminals and verify proper terminal tension.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect all PDM harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the when monitored and set conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete. Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1f04-11 mirror fold control - circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1F04-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">MIRROR FOLD CONTROL - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">On-demand.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module detects a short to ground on the Mirror Fold or Unfold Driver circuit.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Mirror is inoperative.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>MIRROR FOLD DRIVER CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>MIRROR UNFOLD DRIVER CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>DRIVER OUTSIDE REARVIEW MIRROR</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, record and erase the Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Operate the Mirror Fold switch several times.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition from on to off three times.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (P692) PASSENGER MIRROR UNFOLD DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror (Component Side) connector from the PDM C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (P692) Passenger Mirror Unfold Driver circuit at the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror (Component Side) connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (P692) Passenger Mirror Unfold Driver circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P692) Passenger Mirror Unfold Driver circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (P695) PASSENGER MIRROR FOLD DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (P695) Passenger Mirror Fold Driver circuit at the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror (Component Side) connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (P695) Passenger Mirror Fold Driver circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P695) Passenger Mirror Fold Driver circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (P692) PASSENGER MIRROR UNFOLD DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO THE (C170) PASSENGER MIRROR HEATER RETURN CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (P692) Passenger Mirror Unfold Driver circuit and the (C170) Passenger Mirror Heater Return circuit at the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror (Component Side) connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (P692) Passenger Mirror Unfold Driver circuit and the (C170) Passenger Mirror Heater Return circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P692) Passenger Mirror Unfold Driver circuit for a short to the (C170) Passenger Mirror Heater Return circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (P695) PASSENGER MIRROR FOLD DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO THE (C170) PASSENGER MIRROR HEATER RETURN CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (P695) Passenger Mirror Fold Driver circuit and the (C170) Passenger Mirror Heater Return circuit at the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror (Component Side) connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (P695) Passenger Mirror Fold Driver circuit and the (C170) Passenger Mirror Heater Return circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P695) Passenger Mirror Fold Driver circuit for a short to the (C170) Passenger Mirror Heater Return circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>MODULE OR MIRROR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror (Component Side) C1 connector from the PDM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, record and erase the Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Operate the Mirror Fold switch several times.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Operate the mirror switch in all directions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the ignition from on to off three times.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, read the PDM DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check for a CHANGE in the DTCs.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display; B1F04-15-MIRROR FOLD CONTROL - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY OR OPEN as active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Outside Rearview Mirror in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MIRROR, OUTSIDE REARVIEW, GLASS, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module (PDM) in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1f04-15 mirror fold control - circuit short to battery or open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1F04-15</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">MIRROR FOLD CONTROL - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY OR OPEN</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية أو دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">On-demand.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module detects an open or a short to battery on the Mirror Fold or Unfold Driver circuit.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The ability of the Mirror to fold or unfold is inoperative.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>MIRROR FOLD DRIVER CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>MIRROR UNFOLD DRIVER CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>DRIVER OUTSIDE REARVIEW MIRROR SHORTED</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, record and erase the Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>For vehicles equipped with heated mirrors, turn the rear defogger ON.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Operate the Mirror Fold switch several times.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE MIRROR AND HARNESS FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Gain access to the Passenger Door Module but do not disconnect the connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With a 12-volt test light, back probe and connect one lead to the (P695) Passenger Mirror Unfold Driver Circuit and the other lead to the (C17) Passenger Mirror Heater Driver circuit in the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror (Component Side) connector (PDM C2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>While switching the mirror fold control switch fold and unfold, observe the test light.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly when the switch is moved in either direction?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Outside Rearview Mirror Assembly in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to MIRROR, OUTSIDE REARVIEW, GLASS, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1f05-11 electrochromatic mirror control circuit - short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1F05-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ELECTROCHROMATIC MIRROR CONTROL CIRCUIT - SHORT TO GROUND</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The driver electrochromatic mirror is controlled by the Body Control Module (BCM). The BCM receives the dimming control from the sensor in the Interior Rearview Mirror. The BCM send a Bus message to the Passenger Door Module (PDM) which turns the dimming on and off. At night the dimming will be cancelled when the vehicle is in reverse.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The Bus is awake.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The park lamps are turned on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Body Control Module sends a command to the Door Module to turn the Day/Night dimming on and the Electrochromatic Mirror circuit is shorted to ground.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electrochromatic Mirror is inoperative.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ELECTROCHROMATIC MIRROR CONTROL CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>ELECTROCHROMATIC MIRROR CONTROL CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE</li><li>ELECTROCHROMATIC MIRROR RETURN CIRCUIT</li><li>ELECTROCHROMATIC MIRROR CONTROL CIRCUIT SHORTED TO ANOTHER GROUND OR</li><li>RETURN CIRCUIT</li><li>EXTERIOR MIRROR</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, record and erase the DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Block the Light Sensor in the Interior Rearview Mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Shift the transmission to Drive (engine not running)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Wait two minutes.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is this DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (P137) PASSENGER AUTO DAY/NIGHT MIRROR SIGNAL CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror (C1) harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (P137) Passenger Auto Day/Night Mirror Signal at the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror (C1) harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (P137) Passenger Auto Day/Night Mirror Signal?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P137) Passenger Auto Day/Night Mirror Signal circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (P137) PASSENGER AUTO DAY/NIGHT MIRROR SIGNAL CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO THE (P138) PASSENGER AUTO DAY/NIGHT MIRROR RETURN CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (P137) Passenger Auto Day/Night Mirror Signal circuit and the (P138) Passenger Auto Day/Night Mirror Return circuit at the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror (C1) harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (P137) Passenger Auto Day/Night Mirror Signal circuit and the (P138) Passenger Auto Day/Night Mirror Return circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P137) Passenger Auto Day/Night Mirror Signal circuit for a short to the (P138) Passenger Auto Day/Night Mirror Return circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (P137) PASSENGER AUTO DAY/NIGHT MIRROR SIGNAL CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO ANOTHER CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (P137) Passenger Auto Day/Night Mirror Signal circuit and another circuit in the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror (C1) harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (P137) Passenger Auto Day/Night Mirror Signal circuit and another circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P137) Passenger Auto Day/Night Mirror Signal circuit for a short to another circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1f05-12 electrochromatic mirror control circuit - short to battery\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1F05-12</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ELECTROCHROMATIC MIRROR CONTROL CIRCUIT - SHORT TO BATTERY</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The driver electrochromatic mirror is controlled by the Body Control Module (BCM). The BCM receives the dimming control from the sensor in the Interior Rearview Mirror. The BCM send a Bus message to the Passenger Door Module (PDM) which turns the dimming on and off. At night the dimming will be cancelled when the vehicle is in reverse.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The Bus is awake.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The park lamps are turned on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Body Control Module sends a command to the Door Module to turn the Day/Night dimming on and the Electrochromatic Mirror Signal circuit is shorted to voltage.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electrochromatic Mirror is damaged.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electrochromatic Mirror is at full intensity.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ELECTROCHROMATIC MIRROR CONTROL CIRCUIT SHORTED TO BATTERY</li><li>ELECTROCHROMATIC MIRROR RETURN CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>ELECTROCHROMATIC MIRROR CONTROL CIRCUIT SHORTED TO ANOTHER SIGNAL OR</li><li>DRIVER CIRCUIT</li><li>EXTERIOR MIRROR</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, record and erase the DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Block the Light Sensor in the Interior Rearview Mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Shift the transmission to Drive (engine not running)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Wait two minutes.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (P137) PASSENGER AUTO DAY/NIGHT MIRROR SIGNAL CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO BATTERY</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror (C1) harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (P137) Passenger Auto Day/Night Mirror Signal circuit at the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror (C1) harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage above 0.8 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P137) Passenger Auto Day/Night Mirror Signal circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE RESISTANCE BETWEEN THE (P137) PASSENGER AUTO DAY/NIGHT MIRROR SIGNAL CIRCUIT AND THE (P138) PASSENGER AUTO DAY/NIGHT MIRROR RETURN CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (P137) Passenger Auto Day/Night Mirror Signal circuit and the (P138) Passenger Auto Day/Night Mirror Return circuit at the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror (C1) harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance above 100.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P137) Passenger Auto Day/Night Mirror Signal circuit and (P138) Passenger Auto Day/Night Mirror Return circuit for high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (P137) PASSENGER AUTO DAY/NIGHT MIRROR SIGNAL CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO ANOTHER SIGNAL OR DRIVER CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (P137) Passenger Auto Day/Night Mirror Signal circuit and all Signal or Driver circuits at the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror (C1) harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (P137) Passenger Auto Day/Night Mirror Signal circuit and any Signal or Driver circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P137) Passenger Auto Day/Night Mirror Signal circuit for a short to another Signal or Driver circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1f05-13 electrochromatic mirror control circuit - open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1F05-13</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ELECTROCHROMATIC MIRROR CONTROL CIRCUIT - OPEN</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The driver electrochromatic mirror is controlled by the Body Control Module (BCM). The BCM receives the dimming control from the sensor in the Interior Rearview Mirror. The BCM send a Bus message to the Passenger Door Module (PDM) which turns the dimming on and off. At night the dimming will be cancelled when the vehicle is in reverse.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The Bus is awake.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The park lamps are turned on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Body Control Module sends a command to the Door Module to turn the Day/Night dimming on and the Electrochromatic Mirror Signal circuit is open.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electrochromatic Mirror is inoperative.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ELECTROCHROMATIC MIRROR CONTROL CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>EXTERIOR MIRROR</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, record and erase the DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Block the Light Sensor in the Interior Rearview Mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Shift the transmission to Drive (engine not running).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Wait two minutes.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (P137) PASSENGER AUTO DAY/NIGHT MIRROR SIGNAL CIRCUIT AND THE (P138) PASSENGER AUTO DAY/NIGHT MIRROR RETURN CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror (C1) harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (P137) Passenger Auto Day/Night Mirror Signal circuit and (P138) Passenger Auto Day/Night Mirror Return circuit at the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror (C1) harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            The resistance should clock up from approximately 25.0 Ohms to approximately 60.0 Ohms in about 10 seconds.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the resistance clock up and stay under 100.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P137) Passenger Auto Day/Night Mirror Signal / (P138) Passenger Auto Day/Night Mirror Return circuit(s) for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>MIRROR OR MODULE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Replace the Mirror in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MIRROR, OUTSIDE REARVIEW, GLASS, REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, record and erase the DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Block the Light Sensor in the Interior Rearview Mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Shift the transmission to Drive (engine not running).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Wait two minutes.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1f06-12 mirror control sensor position circuit - circuit short to battery\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1F06-12</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">MIRROR CONTROL SENSOR POSITION CIRCUIT - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The mirror position sensor is used in conjunction with the memory system. Anytime the mirror changes position, the sensor changes its value. That value is stored in the door module. When a command from the memory set switch is received, the module will position the mirror to the exact position chosen by the particular driver.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Continuous.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module senses a short to battery on either the 5-volt supply, the mirror horizontal signal or the mirror vertical position signal circuit.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Memory Mirror is disabled.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Mirror will not tilt in reverse.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>MIRROR VERTICAL POSITION SIGNAL CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>MIRROR HORIZONTAL POSITION SIGNAL CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>5 VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>DRIVER OUTSIDE REARVIEW MIRROR</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Before proceeding be sure this vehicle is equipped with Memory Mirrors and the configuration is set to = True.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using a scan tool, record and erase the Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the passenger side turn signal on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the approach lamps on, if equipped.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the rear defogger on, if equipped with heated mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Press and release the Mirror Select switch to select the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Operate the Mirror Adjust Switch in all directions several times while monitoring the scan tool for DTCs in the PDM.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            After adjusting the mirror in one direction wait at least two seconds before adjusting the mirror in the opposite direction, as this will allow time for an active DTC to set, if present.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (A857) 5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO BATTERY</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           In this step we are measuring the 5-Volt Supply voltage at the Passenger Door Module. It should not be over 5.5 volts.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror C1 and C2 (Component Side) harness connectors from the Passenger Door Module C1 and C2 connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage between Ground and the (A857) 5-volt Supply circuit at the Passenger Door Module connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the Voltage above 5.5 Volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (A857) 5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO ANOTHER SIGNAL OR DRIVER CIRCUITS</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           We are now checking the wiring and the mirror for any crossed circuits.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check for continuity between the (A857) 5-Volt Supply circuit and all Signal or Driver circuits in the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror C1 and C2 (Component Side) harness connectors.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (A857) 5-Volt Supply circuit and any Signal or Driver circuit(s)?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (A857) 5-Volt Supply circuit for a short to any Signal or Driver circuit(s).</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (P64) PASSENGER MIRROR VERTICAL POSITION SIGNAL CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO ANOTHER SIGNAL OR DRIVER CIRCUITS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (P64) Passenger Mirror Vertical Position Signal circuit and any Signal or Driver circuits in the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror C1 and C2 (Component Side) harness connectors.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (P64) Passenger Mirror Vertical Position Signal circuit and any Signal or Driver circuit(s)?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P64) Passenger Mirror Vertical Position Signal circuit for a short to any Signal or Driver circuit(s).</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK (P68) PASSENGER MIRROR HORIZONTAL POSITION SIGNAL CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO ANY CIRCUIT DRIVER OR SIGNAL CIRCUITS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (P68) Passenger Mirror Horizontal Position Signal circuit and any Signal or Driver circuits in the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror C1 and C2 (Component Side) harness connectors.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (P68) Passenger Mirror Horizontal Position Signal circuit and any Signal or Driver circuit(s)?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P68) Passenger Mirror Horizontal Position Signal circuit for a short to any Signal or Driver circuit(s).</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1f06-14 mirror control sensor position circuit - circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1F06-14</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">MIRROR CONTROL SENSOR POSITION CIRCUIT - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">OR OPEN</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The mirror position sensor is used in conjunction with the memory system. Anytime the mirror changes position, the sensor changes its value. That value is stored in the door module. When a command from the memory set switch is received, the module will position the mirror to the exact position chosen by the particular driver.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Continuous.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module senses an open or short to ground on either the 5-volt supply, the mirror horizontal signal or the mirror vertical position signal circuit.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Memory Mirror is disabled.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Mirror will not tilt in reverse.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>MIRROR VERTICAL POSITION SIGNAL CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>MIRROR HORIZONTAL POSITION SIGNAL CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>5 VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>DRIVER OUTSIDE REARVIEW MIRROR</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using a scan tool, record and erase the Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the passenger side turn signal on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the approach lamps on, if equipped.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the rear defogger on, if equipped with heated mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Press and release the Mirror Select switch to select the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Operate the Mirror Adjust Switch in all directions several times while monitoring the scan tool for DTCs in the PDM.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           After adjusting the mirror in one direction wait at least two seconds before adjusting the mirror in the opposite direction, as this will allow time for an active DTC to set, if present.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (A857) FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror C1 and C2 (Component Side) harness connectors from the Passenger Door Module C1 and C2 connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (A857) Fused B(+) circuit at the Passenger Door Module (Module Side) connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the Voltage above 11.5 Volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (A857) FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO ANY GROUND OR RETURN CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (A857) Fused B(+) circuit and any designated ground and return circuits at the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror C1 and C2 (Component Side) connectors.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (A857) Fused B(+) circuit and any designated ground and return circuit(s)?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (A857) Fused B(+) circuit for a short to the ground or return circuit(s).</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (P64) PASSENGER MIRROR VERTICAL POSITION SIGNAL CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (P64) Passenger Mirror Vertical Position Signal circuit at the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (P64) Passenger Mirror Vertical Position Signal circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P64) Passenger Mirror Vertical Position Signal circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (P64) PASSENGER MIRROR VERTICAL POSITION SIGNAL CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO ANY GROUND OR RETURN CIRCUITS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (P64) Passenger Mirror Vertical Position Signal circuit (C1- Cavity 7) and any ground or return circuits in the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror C1 and C2 (Component Side) harness connectors.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (P64) Passenger Mirror Vertical Position Signal circuit (C1- Cavity 7) and any ground or return circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P64) Passenger Mirror Vertical Position Signal circuit for a short to any ground or return circuits.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 6</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK THE (P68) PASSENGER MIRROR HORIZONTAL POSITION SIGNAL CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (P68) Passenger Mirror Horizontal Position Signal circuit at the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (P68) Passenger Mirror Horizontal Position Signal circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P68) Passenger Mirror Horizontal Position Signal circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>CHECK THE (P68) PASSENGER MIRROR HORIZONTAL POSITION SIGNAL CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO ANY GROUND OR RETURN CIRCUITS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (P68) Passenger Mirror Horizontal Position Signal circuit and any ground or return circuits at the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror C1 and C2 (Component Side) harness connectors.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (P68) Passenger Mirror Horizontal Position Signal circuit and any ground or return circuit(s)?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P68) Passenger Mirror Horizontal Position Signal circuit for a short to any ground or return circuit(s).</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 8</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>CHECK THE MIRROR OR MODULE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Replace the Outside Rearview Mirror Assembly in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MIRROR, OUTSIDE REARVIEW, GLASS, REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using a scan tool, record and erase the Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the passenger side turn signal on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the approach lamps on, if equipped.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the rear defogger on, if equipped with heated mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Press and release the Mirror Select switch to select the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Operate the Mirror Adjust Switch in all directions several times while monitoring the scan tool for DTCs in the PDM.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           After adjusting the mirror in one direction wait at least two seconds before adjusting the mirror in the opposite direction, as this will allow time for an active DTC to set, if present.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b210c-16 battery voltage input - circuit voltage below threshold\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B210C-16</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">BATTERY VOLTAGE INPUT - CIRCUIT VOLTAGE BELOW THRESHOLD</small><small>العطل: فولتية الدائرة أقل من الحد</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The microprocessor-based electronic Passenger Door Module (PDM) contains logic circuits that monitor various hard wired low current, multiplexed inputs from the power window, power lock, power mirror and memory switches. The program logic within the PDM allows the microprocessor to prioritize all inputs and then determine the tasks it needs to perform. These tasks are then completed either by controlling hard wired outputs to the various motors, actuators or lamps on its own or by sending electronic message requests over the CAN- IHS Bus to the appropriate electronic module in the vehicle.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Continuous.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module detects a voltage input below 9.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Mirror, Window and Lamp functions are disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>POSSIBLE CAUSES</li><li>CHARGING SYSTEM DTC</li><li>FUSED B (+) CIRCUIT HAS HIGH RESISTANCE</li><li>GROUND CIRCUIT HAS HIGH RESISTANCE</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read PCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any PCM Charging or Battery DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the PCM DTC(s). Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE PASSENGER DOOR MODULE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Start the engine and run for two minutes.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (A925) FUSED B(+) OR (Z917) GROUND CIRCUITS FOR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Door Module C3 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to the (Z917) Ground circuit, check the (A925) Fused B(+) circuit at the Passenger Door Module C3 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test the Fused B(+) and the Ground circuits to determine which one has the high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the circuit for high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b210c-17 battery voltage input - circuit voltage above threshold\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B210C-17</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">BATTERY VOLTAGE INPUT - CIRCUIT VOLTAGE ABOVE THRESHOLD</small><small>العطل: فولتية الدائرة أعلى من الحد</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The microprocessor-based electronic Passenger Door Module (PDM) contains logic circuits that monitor various hard wired low current, multiplexed inputs from the power window, power lock, power mirror and memory switches. The program logic within the PDM allows the microprocessor to prioritize all inputs and then determine the tasks it needs to perform. These tasks are then completed either by controlling hard wired outputs to the various motors, actuators or lamps on its own or by sending electronic message requests over the CAN- IHS Bus to the appropriate electronic module in the vehicle.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Continuous.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module detects voltage input above 16.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Mirror, Window and Lamp functions are disabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>POSSIBLE CAUSES</li><li>HIGH VOLTAGE POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTC</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read PCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any PCM Charging or Battery DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the PCM DTC(s). Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE PASSENGER DOOR MODULE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the engine and run for two minutes.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b21dd-84 system voltage - signal below allowable range\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B21DD-84</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SYSTEM VOLTAGE - SIGNAL BELOW ALLOWABLE RANGE</small><small>العطل: الإشارة أقل من المدى المسموح</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The microprocessor-based electronic Passenger Door Module (PDM) contains logic circuits that monitor</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">various hard wired low current, multiplexed inputs from the power window, power lock, power mirror and memory switches. The program logic within the PDM allows the microprocessor to prioritize all inputs and then determine the tasks it needs to perform. These tasks are then completed either by controlling hard wired outputs to the various motors, actuators or lamps on its own or by sending electronic message requests over the CAN- IHS Bus to the appropriate electronic module in the vehicle.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The Bus is awake.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module receives a Controller Area Network (CAN) message from the Body Control Module (BCM) that the battery voltage was below 10 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>LOW BATTERY SYSTEM VOLTAGE</li><li>BATTERY OR CHARGING SYSTEM</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read BCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are there any BCM Charging or Battery DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TESTING FOR AN INTERMITTENT CONDITION procedure. Refer to TESTING FOR AN INTERMITTENT CONDITION . This code is for information only. At some time there was low battery system voltage. Check the battery and charging system in accordance with the Service Information.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b21dd-85 system voltage - signal above allowable range\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B21DD-85</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SYSTEM VOLTAGE - SIGNAL ABOVE ALLOWABLE RANGE</small><small>العطل: الإشارة أعلى من المدى المسموح</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The microprocessor-based electronic Passenger Door Module (PDM) contains logic circuits that monitor various hard wired low current, multiplexed inputs from the power window, power lock, power mirror and memory switches. The program logic within the PDM allows the microprocessor to prioritize all inputs and then determine the tasks it needs to perform. These tasks are then completed either by controlling hard wired outputs to the various motors, actuators or lamps on its own or by sending electronic message requests over the CAN- IHS Bus to the appropriate electronic module in the vehicle.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The Bus is awake.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module receives a Controller Area Network (CAN) message from the Body Control Module (BCM) that the battery voltage was above 16 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>HIGH BATTERY SYSTEM VOLTAGE</li><li>CHARGING SYSTEM</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read BCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are there any BCM Charging or Battery DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TESTING FOR AN INTERMITTENT CONDITION procedure. Refer to TESTING FOR AN INTERMITTENT CONDITION . This code is for information only. At some time there was high battery system voltage. Check the battery and charging system in accordance with the Service Information.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b224f-54 door module internal - missing calibration\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B224F-54</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DOOR MODULE INTERNAL - MISSING CALIBRATION</small><small>العطل: المعايرة مفقودة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The microprocessor-based electronic Passenger Door Module (PDM) contains logic circuits that monitor various hard wired low current, multiplexed inputs from the power window, power lock, power mirror and memory switches. The program logic within the PDM allows the microprocessor to prioritize all inputs and then determine the tasks it needs to perform. These tasks are then completed either by controlling hard wired outputs to the various motors, actuators or lamps on its own or by sending electronic message requests over the CAN- IHS Bus to the appropriate electronic module in the vehicle.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Continuous.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module has lost the parameters for full up and down window travel.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">No window express operation.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>OTHER DTCS SET IN THIS MODULE</li><li>MODULE NOT CALIBRATED</li><li>POWER WINDOW MOTOR</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR RELATED DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, read the PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display any window control circuit, window position sensor or battery voltage DTCs?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Diagnose and repair the other DTCs in this module before proceeding.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Operate the Passenger Window up and down several times.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Wait 30 seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>RESET THE WINDOW MODULE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool in the Vehicle View screen, select the Diagnostic Procedures tab and perform the &quot;Reset ECU&quot; routine to the Door Module.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>After the ECU reset routine is completed, start the engine or connect a battery charger and set at charging voltage.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Sit in the driver seat and close the doors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the window switch, move the passenger window part way down.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Using the window switch, raise the window to the full up position and continue to hold the switch for an additional two seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Lower the window to the full down position by pushing down on the window switch to its second detent and continue to hold the switch for an additional two seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Lift the window switch to the express up position and release.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the window move to the full up position?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b224f-96 door module internal - component internal failure\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B224F-96</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DOOR MODULE INTERNAL - COMPONENT INTERNAL FAILURE</small><small>العطل: عطل داخلي بالمكوّن</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The microprocessor-based electronic Passenger Door Module (PDM) contains logic circuits that monitor various hard wired low current, multiplexed inputs from the power window, power lock, power mirror and memory switches. The program logic within the PDM allows the microprocessor to prioritize all inputs and then determine the tasks it needs to perform. These tasks are then completed either by controlling hard wired outputs to the various motors, actuators or lamps on its own or by sending electronic message requests over the CAN- IHS Bus to the appropriate electronic module in the vehicle.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Latching.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module detects an internal failure.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">An incorrect window/mirror/lamp/lock/switch operation.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, read the Door Module DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the DTC active or stored?</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST . Review the Vehicle Scan Report and Repair any other DTCs that have set with the appropriate procedure in Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b25af-2a door lock/unlock switch - stuck\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B25AF-2A</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DOOR LOCK/UNLOCK SWITCH - STUCK</small><small>العطل: عالق (Stuck)</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The microprocessor-based electronic Passenger Door Module (PDM) contains logic circuits that monitor various hard wired low current, multiplexed inputs from the power window, power lock, power mirror and memory switches. The program logic within the PDM allows the microprocessor to prioritize all inputs and then determine the tasks it needs to perform. These tasks are then completed either by controlling hard wired outputs to the various motors, actuators or lamps on its own or by sending electronic message requests over the CAN- IHS Bus to the appropriate electronic module in the vehicle.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">On-demand.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Passenger Door Lock/Unlock switch is stuck for more than 30 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Incorrect lock/unlock operation. All other switches operate normally.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>PASSENGER WINDOW/DOOR LOCK SWITCH FAULTY WIRING</li><li>PASSENGER WINDOW/DOOR LOCK SWITCH STICKING</li><li>PASSENGER DOOR MODULE (PDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Operate the Passenger Door Lock Switch in all positions several times.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on and wait 30 seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE DOOR LOCK SWITCH</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the Passenger Window/Door Lock Switch stick?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Window/Door Lock Switch in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SWITCH, LOCK, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b25b0-31 window position sensor - no signal\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B25B0-31</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">WINDOW POSITION SENSOR - NO SIGNAL</small><small>العطل: لا توجد إشارة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The window motor contains a hall effect sensor to detect the window position. A hall effect sensor is a transducer that varies its output voltage in response to changes in magnetic field. If the motor loses its counts, it may perform erratically or in very short movements.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">On-demand.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module senses one of the window motor hall sensors does not generate a signal during a window movement.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">No window express operation. Window is in step motion only.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>WINDOW HALL SENSOR SUPPLY CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>WINDOW HALL SENSOR A SIGNAL CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>WINDOW HALL SENSOR RETURN CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>PASSENGER WINDOW MOTOR</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Operate the Passenger Window up and down several times.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Wait 30 seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (Q302) PASSENGER WINDOW HALL SENSOR A SIGNAL CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Door Module C4 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (Q302) Passenger Window Hall Sensor A Signal circuit between the Passenger Door Module C4 connector and the Passenger Window Motor harness connector at the Passenger Door Module C4 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 2.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the (Q302) Passenger Window Hall Sensor A Signal circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (Q302) PASSENGER WINDOW HALL SENSOR A SIGNAL CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Door Module C4 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (Q302) Passenger Window Hall Sensor A Signal circuit at the Passenger Door Module C4 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (Q302) Passenger Window Hall Sensor A Signal circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the (Q302) Passenger Window Hall Sensor A Signal circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (Q302) PASSENGER WINDOW HALL SENSOR A SIGNAL CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO ANOTHER CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The ignition must be off when performing a resistance check to find a short between circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Isolate the circuit by disconnecting the Passenger Door Module (PDM) and every component harness connector containing the circuit being tested. At this time leave all in-line connectors connected. Note: Use the wiring diagram as a guide to follow the path of the circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect one lead of the DVOM to the circuit being tested at the PDM harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the other lead of the DVOM probe all other circuits at the PDM harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           With the circuit isolated there should be no continuity between the circuit being tested and any other circuit.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the circuit being tested and any other circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the short between the circuits that have continuity. Use the wiring diagram as a guide to trace the circuits and look for any in-line connectors to help isolate the location of the short.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all PDM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity. Check for spread terminals and verify proper terminal tension.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect all PDM harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the when monitored and set conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the WINDOW MOTOR REGULATOR. Refer to MOTOR, WINDOW REGULATOR, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b25b1-11 window position sensor power supply - circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B25B1-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">WINDOW POSITION SENSOR POWER SUPPLY - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The microprocessor-based electronic Passenger Door Module (PDM) contains logic circuits that monitor various hard wired low current, multiplexed inputs from the power window, power lock, power mirror and memory switches. The program logic within the PDM allows the microprocessor to prioritize all inputs and then determine the tasks it needs to perform. These tasks are then completed either by controlling hard wired outputs to the various motors, actuators or lamps on its own or by sending electronic message requests over the CAN- IHS Bus to the appropriate electronic module in the vehicle.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">WHEN MONITORED AND SET CONDITIONS</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The Bus is awake.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The Door Ajar signal is not ajar.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Set Conditions:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The Passenger Door Module senses the Passenger Window Drop (Pawl) Switch stuck for over 30 seconds.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">DOOR HANDLE (INSIDE OR OUTSIDE) STICKING PASSENGER WINDOW DROP SWITCH SENSE CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND PASSENGER DOOR LATCH ASSEMBLY PASSENGER DOOR MODULE (PDM)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">On-demand.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module senses the Window Hall Sensor Supply circuit is shorted to ground.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">No window express operation. Window in step motion only.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>WINDOW HALL SENSOR SUPPLY CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>DRIVER WINDOW MOTOR</li><li>DRIVER</li><li>DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Open and close the Passenger door several times from the outside and inside handles.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Wait 30 seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE DOOR HANDLE (INSIDE OR OUTSIDE) FOR STICKING</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Open and close the Passenger door several times from the outside and inside handles.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does either handle tend to stick?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair or replace the cause for the sticking handle (or latch).</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE PASSENGER DOOR LATCH ASSEMBLY</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, erase the DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Door Latch connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Latch Assembly in accordance with Service Information. Refer to LATCH, DOOR, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (Q58) PASSENGER WINDOW DROP SWITCH SENSE CIRCUIT FOR A</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">SHORTED TO GROUND</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Door Module C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (Q58) Passenger Window Drop Switch Sense circuit.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (Q58) Passenger Window Drop Switch Sense circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair the (Q58) Passenger Window Drop Switch Sense circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b285e-11 window switch backlighting - circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B285E-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">WINDOW SWITCH BACKLIGHTING - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The bus is awake.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The park lamps are on.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The window lock out switch is on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module detects the Passenger Window Switch Illumination Driver circuit is shorted to ground.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Incorrect lamp operation. All other switch functions operate normally.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>PASSENGER WINDOW SWITCH ILLUMINATION DRIVER CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</li><li>PASSENGER WINDOW SWITCH ILLUMINATION DRIVER CIRCUIT SHORT TO THE</li><li>PASSENGER WINDOW SWITCH RETURN</li><li>WINDOW/DOOR LOCK SWITCH SHORTED</li><li>PASSENGER DOOR MODULE (PDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Ensure the passenger window lock out switch is on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the park lights on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Wait 30 seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE WINDOW/DOOR LOCK SWITCH FOR A SHORT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, erase the DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Window/Door Lock Switch connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Ensure the passenger window lock out switch is on and the park lamps are still on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Wait 30 seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Window/Door Lock Switch in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SWITCH, POWER WINDOW, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (E34) PASSENGER WINDOW SWITCH ILLUMINATION DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the park lamps off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Door Module C5 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for continuity between Ground and the (E34) Passenger Window Switch Illumination Driver circuit.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between Ground and the (E34) Passenger Window Switch Illumination Driver circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (E34) Passenger Window Switch Illumination Driver circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (E34) PASSENGER WINDOW SWITCH ILLUMINATION DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO THE (Q936) PASSENGER WINDOW SWITCH RETURN CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (E34) Passenger Window Switch Illumination Driver circuit and the (Q936) Passenger Window Switch Return circuit.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (E34) Passenger Window Switch Illumination Driver circuit and the (Q936) Passenger Window Switch Return circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (E34) Passenger Window Switch Illumination Driver circuit for a short to the (Q936) Passenger Window Switch Return circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b285f-11 blind spot warning light control - circuit short to ground-pass\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B285F-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">BLIND SPOT WARNING LIGHT CONTROL - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND-PASS</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Blind Spot Warning Indicator in each mirror is controlled by its accompanying Door Module. Anytime blind spot detection is unavailable or blocked, the Blind Spot Warning Indicators in both side Mirror LEDs will be illuminated.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Left Blind Spot Sensor (LBSS) is the master module of the Blind Spot Monitor (BSM) system. The LBSS communicates the status of both sensors on the CAN IHS bus to the Radio, Door Modules and Instrument Cluster.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The bus is awake.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The Passenger Door Module configuration for Blind Spot Monitoring is true.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The Blind Spot Indicator is turned on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Passenger Door Module detects the Blind Spot Indicator circuit voltage is below 4.0 volts</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Incorrect lamp operation/lamp off.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>PASSENGER MIRROR ASSEMBLY</li><li>PASSENGER DOOR MODULE (PDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition from on to off three times.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE MIRROR CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Door Module C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Inspect the wiring and connectors between the mirror and the Passenger Door Module.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE MIRROR ASSEMBLY</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase the DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition from on to off three times.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is DTC B285F-11 set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Outside Rearview Mirror Assembly in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to MIRROR, OUTSIDE REARVIEW, GLASS, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b285f-15 blind spot warning light control - circuit short to battery or open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B285F-15</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">BLIND SPOT WARNING LIGHT CONTROL - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY OR OPEN</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية أو دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Blind Spot Warning Indicator in each mirror is controlled by its accompanying Door Module. Anytime blind spot detection is unavailable or blocked, the Blind Spot Warning Indicators in both side Mirror LEDs will be illuminated.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Left Blind Spot Sensor (LBSS) is the master module of the Blind Spot Monitor (BSM) system. The LBSS communicates the status of both sensors on the CAN IHS bus to the Radio, Door Modules and Instrument Cluster.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">On-demand.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module detects the Blind Spot Indicator circuit is shorted to voltage or open.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Incorrect Lamp operation/Lamp on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>DRIVER OUTSIDE REARVIEW MIRROR</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition from on to off three times.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>INSPECT MIRROR CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passengers Door Module C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Inspect the wiring and connectors between the mirror and the Passengers Door Module.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE MIRROR ASSEMBLY</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (P554) Passenger Mirror Approach/Blindspot Lamp Return circuit and the (P712) Passenger Blind Spot Indicator Driver circuit in the PDM C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the resistance between 550.0 and 650.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Outside Rearview Mirror Assembly in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to MIRROR, OUTSIDE REARVIEW, GLASS, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b2860-11 door ambient light control - circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B2860-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DOOR AMBIENT LIGHT CONTROL - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">An ambient lamp can be a: map pocket, door handle, halo ring, cup holder, etc. It is a LED with a built in circuit board. The Body Control Module sends a command to the Door Module to turn it on or off.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The Bus is awake.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The Ambient Lamp is commanded to be on.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The Door Module configuration is correct.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module detects the Door Ambient Lamp Driver circuit is shorted to ground.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Incorrect lamp operation/lamp off.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>PASSENGER DOOR AMBIENT LAMP DRIVER CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>PASSENGER DOOR AMBIENT LAMP DRIVER CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE DOOR LIGHTING</li><li>RETURN CIRCUIT</li><li>PASSENGER DOOR HANDLE LAMP</li><li>PASSENGER MAP POCKET LAMP</li><li>PASSENGER DOOR MODULE (PDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          It is recommended that a battery charger be connected and set on low during this test.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Be sure the thumbwheel on the Dimmer Module are turned fully on during this test.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on to off three times and leave in the Lock position.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the park lamps on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Wait one minute.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE PASSENGER DOOR HANDLE LAMP FOR A SHORT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, erase the DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Remove the inner door panel trim in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Make sure the Passenger Door Handle Lamp connector is disconnected.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Re-connect the Passenger Door Map Pocket Lamp connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Be sure the park lamps are still on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Wait one minute.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Handle Lamp Assembly in Accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE PASSENGER DOOR MAP POCKET LAMP FOR A SHORT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, erase the DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Door Map Pocket Lamp connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Be sure the park lamps are still on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Wait one minute.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Map Pocket Lamp Assembly in Accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (M35) PASSENGER DOOR AMBIENT LAMP FEED CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Door Module C5 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between Ground and the (M35) Passenger Door Ambient Lamp Feed circuit at the PDM C5 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between Ground and the (M35) Passenger Door Ambient Lamp Feed circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (M35) Passenger Door Ambient Lamp Feed circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (M35) PASSENGER DOOR AMBIENT LAMP FEED CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO THE (M36) PASSENGER DOOR LIGHTING RETURN CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (M35) Passenger Door Ambient Lamp Feed circuit and the (M36) Passenger Door Lighting Return circuit at the PDM C5 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (M35) Passenger Door Ambient Lamp Feed circuit and the (M36) Passenger Door Lighting Return circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (M35) Passenger Door Ambient Lamp Feed circuit for a short to the (M36) Passenger Door Lighting Return circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in Accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b2860-15 door ambient light control - circuit short to battery or open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B2860-15</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DOOR AMBIENT LIGHT CONTROL - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY OR OPEN</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية أو دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">An ambient lamp can be a: map pocket, door handle, halo ring, cup holder, etc. It is a LED with a built in circuit board. The Body Control Module controls the operation and sends a bus message to the Door Module to turn the lamps on or off.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">WHEN MONITORED AND SET CONDITIONS</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The Bus is awake.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The Ambient Lamp is commanded to be on.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The Door Module configuration is correct.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Set Conditions:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The Door Module detects the Door Ambient Lamp Driver circuit is shorted to battery or open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Default Actions:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Incorrect lamp operation/ lamp on.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">PASSENGER DOOR AMBIENT LAMP DRIVER CIRCUIT SHORTED TO BATTERY VOLTAGE</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">PASSENGER DOOR AMBIENT LAMP DRIVER CIRCUIT OPEN PASSENGER DOOR MAP POCKET LAMP PASSENGER DOOR HANDLE LAMP PASSENGER DOOR MODULE (PDM)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Be sure the thumbwheel on the Dimmer Module are turned fully on during this test.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on to off three times and leave the ignition in the Lock position.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the park lamps on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the ignition on and wait one minute.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (M35) PASSENGER DOOR AMBIENT LAMP DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Remove the inner door panel trim in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to PANEL, DOOR TRIM, REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Leave the Passenger Door Map Pocket and Handle Lamp connectors connected.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Door Module C5 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (M35) Passenger Door Ambient Lamp Driver circuit in the Passenger Door Module C5 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (M35) Passenger Door Ambient Lamp Driver circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (M35) PASSENGER DOOR AMBIENT LAMP DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Be sure the Passenger Door Map Pocket and Door Handle Lamp connectors are still connected.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Connect a fused jumper wire between B(+) and the (M35) Passenger Door Ambient Lamp Driver circuit in the PDM C5 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect a jumper wire between ground and the (M36) Passenger Door Lighting Return circuit in the PDM C5 harness connector</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the Passenger Door Map Pocket and Handle Lamps illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (M35) PASSENGER DOOR AMBIENT LAMP DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off and remove both jumper wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Door Map Pocket and Handle Lamp harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (M35) Passenger Door Ambient Lamp Driver circuit between the PDM C5 harness connector, and the harness connectors for the Passenger Door Map Pocket and the Passenger Door Handle Lamps.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 2.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open in the (M35) Passenger Door Courtesy Lamp Driver circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (M36) PASSENGER DOOR LIGHTING RETURN CIRCUIT FOR A OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (M36) Passenger Door Lighting Return circuit between the PDM C5 harness connector and the Passenger Door Map Pocket Lamp harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (M36) Passenger Door Lighting Return circuit between the PDM C5 harness connector and the Passenger Door Handle Lamp harness connectors.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the resistance below 2.0 Ohms on both the Map Pocket and Handle circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Ambient Lamp(s) as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open in the (M36) Passenger Door Lighting Return circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b2861-11 mirror approach light control - circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B2861-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">MIRROR APPROACH LIGHT CONTROL - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Continuous.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module detects a short low on the Approach Lamp Driver circuit for more than two seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Incorrect lamp operation / lamp off.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>DRIVER OUTSIDE REARVIEW MIRROR APPROACH LAMP DRIVER CIRCUIT FAULTY</li><li>WIRING</li><li>DRIVER OUTSIDE REARVIEW MIRROR</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using a scan tool, record and erase Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition off then on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Press and release the Mirror Select switch to select the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Open the passenger door to turn the approach lights on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the passenger side turn signal on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Fold and unfold the mirrors (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Turn the rear defogger on (if equipped with heated mirrors).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Operate the Mirror Adjust switch in all directions several times while monitoring the scan tool for DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           After adjusting the mirror in one direction wait at least two seconds before adjusting the mirror in the opposite direction, as this will allow time for an active fault to set if present.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (P553) PASSENGER MIRROR BLINDSPOT LAMP SUPPLY CIRCUIT FOR A</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">SHORT TO GROUND</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror C1 and C2 (Component Side) harness connectors from the Passenger Door Module.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (P553) Passenger Mirror Blindspot Lamp Supply circuit at the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror C1 (Component Side) connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (P553) Passenger Mirror Blindspot Lamp Supply circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P553) Passenger Mirror Blindspot Lamp Supply circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (P553) PASSENGER MIRROR BLINDSPOT LAMP SUPPLY CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO THE (P554) PASSENGER MIRROR BLINDSPOT LAMP RETURN CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (P553) Passenger Mirror Approach Light Driver circuit and the (P554) Passenger Mirror Approach/Blindspot Lamp Return circuit at the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror C1 (Component Side) harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (P553) Passenger Mirror Approach Light Driver circuit and the (P554) Passenger Mirror Approach/Blindspot Lamp Return circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P553) Passenger Mirror Approach Light Driver circuit for a short to the (P554) Passenger Mirror Approach/Blindspot Lamp Return circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (P553) PASSENGER MIRROR BLINDSPOT LAMP SUPPLY CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO ANY PASSENGER MIRROR GROUND OR RETURN CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (P553) Passenger Mirror Approach Light Driver circuit and each of the Passenger Mirror Ground and Return circuits in the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror C1 and C2 (Component Side) connectors.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (P553) Passenger Mirror Approach Light Driver circuit and each of the Passenger Mirror Ground and Return circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P553) Passenger Mirror Approach Light Driver circuit for a short to any ground or return circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>MIRROR OR MODULE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Replace the Outside Rearview Mirror Assembly in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MIRROR, OUTSIDE REARVIEW, GLASS, REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using a scan tool, record and erase Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition off then on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Press and release the Mirror Select switch to select the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Open the passenger door to turn the approach lights on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the passenger side turn signal on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Fold and unfold the mirrors (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Turn the rear defogger on (if equipped with heated mirrors).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Operate the Mirror Adjust switch in all directions several times while monitoring the scan tool for DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           After adjusting the mirror in one direction wait at least two seconds before adjusting the mirror in the opposite direction, as this will allow time for an active fault to set if present.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b2861-15 mirror approach light control - circuit short to battery or open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B2861-15</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">MIRROR APPROACH LIGHT CONTROL - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY OR OPEN</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية أو دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Continuous.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module detects an open or a short to battery on the Approach Lamp Driver circuit for more than two seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Incorrect lamp operation / lamp on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>DRIVER MIRROR APPROACH LAMP DRIVER CIRCUIT FAULTY WIRING</li><li>DRIVER OUTSIDE REARVIEW MIRROR</li><li>DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using a scan tool, record and erase Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition off then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Open the passenger door to turn the approach lights on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the passenger side turn signal on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Fold and unfold the mirrors (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Turn the rear defogger on (if equipped with heated mirrors).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Operate the Mirror Adjust switch in all directions several times while monitoring the scan tool for DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            After adjusting the mirror in one direction wait at least two seconds before adjusting the mirror in the opposite direction, as this will allow time for an active fault to set if present.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (P553) PASSENGER MIRROR APPROACH LIGHT DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror C1 and C2 (Component Side) harness connectors from the Door Module.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (P553) Passenger Mirror Approach Light Driver circuit in the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror C1 (Component Side) harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P553) Passenger Mirror Approach Light Driver circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (P553) PASSENGER MIRROR APPROACH LIGHT DRIVER CIRCUIT AND THE (P554) PASSENGER MIRROR/APPROACH BLINDSPOT LAMP RETURN FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check for continuity between the (P553) Passenger Mirror Approach Light Driver circuit and the (P554) Passenger Mirror Approach/Blindspot Lamp Return circuit at the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror C1 (Component Side) connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (P553) Passenger Mirror Approach Light Driver circuit and the (P554) Passenger Mirror Approach/Blindspot Lamp Return circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P553) Passenger Mirror Approach Light Driver circuit or the (P554) Passenger Mirror Approach/Blindspot Lamp Return circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (P553) PASSENGER MIRROR APPROACH LIGHT DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO ANOTHER MIRROR DRIVER OR SIGNAL CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (P553) Passenger Mirror Approach Light Driver circuit and any designated Mirror Driver and Signal circuits at the Passenger Outside Rearview Mirror C1 and C2 (Component Side) connectors.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (P553) Passenger Mirror Approach Light Driver circuit and any designated Mirror Driver and Signal circuit(s)?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (P553) Passenger Mirror Approach Light Driver circuit for a short to another designated Mirror Driver and Signal circuit(s).</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>MIRROR OR MODULE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Replace the Outside Rearview Mirror Assembly in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MIRROR, OUTSIDE REARVIEW, GLASS, REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using a scan tool, record and erase Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition off then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Open the passenger door to turn the approach lights on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the passenger side turn signal on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Fold and unfold the mirrors (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Turn the rear defogger on (if equipped with heated mirrors).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Operate the Mirror Adjust switch in all directions several times while monitoring the scan tool for DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          After adjusting the mirror in one direction wait at least two seconds before adjusting the mirror in the opposite direction, as this will allow time for an active fault to set if present.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0010-00 can interior bus\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0010-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CAN INTERIOR BUS</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">For an in-depth explanation of the CAN system operation, Refer to OPERATION .</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The CAN Interior bus is awake.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Door Module detects the CAN Interior Bus (+) circuit is shorted to the CAN Interior Bus (-) circuit.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">All features dependent on the CAN Interior bus will not be available.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">No communication on the CAN Interior bus to a module is possible.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>CAN INTERIOR BUS (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE CAN INTERIOR BUS (-) CIRCUIT</li><li>ANY CAN INTERIOR BUS MODULE</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, create a Vehicle Scan Report and attach it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, read PDM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the U0010-00 CAN Interior Bus diagnostic procedure in the BCM. Refer to U0010-00- CAN INTERIOR BUS .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the Stored Lost Communication DTCs diagnostic procedure. Refer to STORED LOST COMMUNICATION DTCS .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0140-00 lost communication with body control module\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0140-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH BODY CONTROL MODULE</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع BODY CONTROL MODULE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0164-00 lost communication with hvac control module\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0164-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH HVAC CONTROL MODULE</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع HVAC CONTROL MODULE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0199-00 lost communication with driver door module\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0199-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH DRIVER DOOR MODULE</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع DRIVER DOOR MODULE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">U0232-00 LOST COMMUNICATION WITH BLIND SPOT DETECTION MODULE</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Article GUID: A00910334</p></div></div></details></div>";
